[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5781116098","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110903#issuecomment-5781116098","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110903","id":5781116098,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWJTUwg","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T17:37:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T17:37:59Z","body":"Godot likely can't load the assembly because the DLL name doesn't match the assembly name from the `dotnet/project/assembly_name` setting[^1]. You can change this in _Project Settings_ to match the value from `<AssemblyName>` but you'll also have to change the name of the `.csproj` and `.sln` files, since Godot uses this name to find them. Although, doing this, then the `<AssemblyName>` property is redundant since by default it matches the name of the `.csproj` file.\n\n[^1]: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0f1b62b707d681eef2fbd8d731642a3e196c4484/modules/mono/mono_gd/gd_mono.cpp#L766-L770","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":